 format="html"><text /></partiallycorrectfeedback><incorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></incorrectfeedback><answer fraction="100.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Leaving the ocean visible makes it unclear whether the speaker has truly put away the journey or still longs for possibility.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Whether maps are made of paper.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Whether oceans are wet.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Whether the poem contains any image.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>CW_U04_L03_R_Q03</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Poem: The mailbox waited with its red flag raised. Which meaning is most reasonable?&lt;/p&gt;</text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text /></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>none</answernumbering><showstandardinstruction>1</showstandardinstruction><correctfeedback format="html"><text /></correctfeedback><partiallycorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></partiallycorrectfeedback><incorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></incorrectfeedback><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The mailbox is literally alive.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="100.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The raised flag and waiting mailbox suggest the speaker expects or hopes for a message.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The flag has no importance.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html">