iguous?&lt;/p&gt;</text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text /></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>none</answernumbering><showstandardinstruction>1</showstandardinstruction><correctfeedback format="html"><text /></correctfeedback><partiallycorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></partiallycorrectfeedback><incorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></incorrectfeedback><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The size of the umbrella only.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="100.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The coincidence between the umbrella and phone call invites suspense without proving a supernatural connection.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Whether phones can ring.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Whether rain exists anywhere.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>CW_U04_L03_R_Q19</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Poem: He swept the porch clean, then left one leaf in the center. Which meaning is most reasonable?&lt;/p&gt;</text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text /></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>none</answernumbering><showstandardinstruction>1</showstandardinstruction><correctfeedback format="html"><text /></correctfeedback><partiallycorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></partiallycorrectfeedback><incorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></incorrectfeedback><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The speaker forgot how to sweep.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The leaf is definitely fake.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="100.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Leaving one leaf may represent a deliberate decision to preserve imperfection or memory.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The porch is a classroom.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>CW_U04_L03_R_Q20</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Poem: The window reflected the sky and the bars at the same time. Which interpretation is strongest?&lt;/p&gt;</text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text /></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>none</answernumbering><showstandardinstruction>1</showstandardinstruction><correctfeedback format="html"><text /></correctfeedback><partiallycorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></partiallycorrectfeedback><incorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></incorrectfeedback><answer fraction="100.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The window holds images of freedom and confinement at once, creating a layered conflict.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The window is not glass.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The poem has no contrast.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The bars prove the speaker is happy.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>CW_U04_L03_R_Q21</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Poem: I buried my shoes beside the path. What should a careful interpretation do?&lt;/p&gt;</text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text /></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>none</answernumbering><showstandardinstruction>1</showstandardinstruction><correctfeedback format="html"><text /></correctfeedback><partiallycorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></partiallycorrectfeedback><incorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></incorrectfeedback><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Claim the speaker can never walk again.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="100.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;A careful interpretation should compare multiple possible meanings and support each claim with details from the line.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Ignore the shoes.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Say the poem is only about dirt.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>CW_U04_L03_R_Q22</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Poem: The empty chair faced the piano all winter. Which meaning is best supported?&lt;/p&gt;</text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text /></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>none</answernumbering><showstandardinstruction>1</showstandardinstruction><correctfeedback format="html"><text /></correctfeedback><partiallycorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></partiallycorrectfeedback><incorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></incorrectfeedback><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The chair is definitely broken.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Winter means the poem is cheerful.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Pianos cannot be in rooms.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="100.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The chair facing the piano suggests absence, waiting, or remembered music during the long winter.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>CW_U04_L03_R_Q23</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Poem: She wore the medal under her shirt. Which ambiguity is strongest?&lt;/p&gt;</text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text /></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>none</answernumbering><showstandardinstruction>1</showstandardinstruction><correctfeedback format="html"><text /></correctfeedback><partiallycorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></partiallycorrectfeedback><incorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></incorrectfeedback><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Whether medals are metal.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Whether shirts are clothing.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="100.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Hiding the medal suggests pride complicated by secrecy, modesty, or discomfort with recognition.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Whether she owns the medal at all.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>CW_U04_L03_R_Q24</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Poem: The calendar still showed April in December. What implied meaning is most reasonable?&lt;/p&gt;</text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text /></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>none</answernumbering><showstandardinstruction>1</showstandardinstruction><correctfeedback format="html"><text /></correctfeedback><partiallycorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></partiallycorrectfeedback><incorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></incorrectfeedback><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;December comes before April.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The calendar is a weather report.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The poem proves the speaker loves math.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="100.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The unchanged calendar suggests the speaker is emotionally fixed in a past moment or has neglected the present.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>CW_U04_L03_R_Q25</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Poem: The boat was tied to shore, but its reflection drifted away. What layered meaning is strongest?&lt;/p&gt;</text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text /></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>none</answernumbering><showstandardinstruction>1</showstandardinstruction><correctfeedback format="html"><text /></correctfeedback><partiallycorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></partiallycorrectfeedback><incorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></incorrectfeedback><answer fraction="100.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The tied boat and drifting reflection create a tension between physical restraint and the desire for freedom.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The boat is definitely sinking.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The reflection is a real second boat.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The shore is moving.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer></question></quiz>